<title>UK: INSIGHT - Europe precious metals mostly seen lower.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT - Europe precious metals mostly seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> SPOT     NY CLOSE  * SUPPORT * RESIST * RSI14 *   MA10 *   MA30</p>
<p> GOLD   342.70/3.30 *  340.00 * 345.00 *    46 * 345.34 * 343.03</p>
<p> SILVER   4.69/4.71 *    4.60 *   4.80 *    42 *   4.78 *   4.74</p>
<p> PLAT   392.00/3.00 *  385.00 * 400.00 *    62 * 391.34 * 378.88</p>
<p>-----------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - May 22---------------</p>
<p>Near-term gold prices are expected to hold a range of between $340.00 and $345.00 an ounce, but are expected to probe lower against the backdrop of down-trending charts.</p>
<p>Silver is also likely to adopt a downside trend, while platinum will struggle to move towards $400 resistance, traders and analysts said.</p>
